Z||000003||JSocha||08-01-2001||09:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Remember the days when our 386s came with huge 120 meg hard discs and your friends would say WOW, you'll never use all of that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damn Straight!  I remember 10 & 20MB and people saying that along with the 386/33Mhz being a nuculear power plant of processing power.  We won't talk about the 8088's and the unknown 8Mhz of those power demons w/green (or RGB) monitors and 128 or 256K of memory!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||08-01-2001||10:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B> Damn Straight!  I remember 10 & 20MB and people saying that along with the 386/33Mhz being a nuculear power plant of processing power.  We won't talk about the 8088's and the unknown 8Mhz of those power demons w/green (or RGB) monitors and 128 or 256K of memory!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mwahahaha<BR>Reminds me of my first computer an AT&T 3600 8086 with dual 5 1/4 drives, 64k memory, 1200 baud modem, BASIC bios and a whopping 20 meg MFM hard drive. Now that was a high tech 3200 dollar piece of equipment, I later put in an RLL controller and bumped the 20 megs capacity to 30  wooohoo now that was major digital realestate!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
